  {
    "id": "spawn.lifecycle.L198.16",
    "file": "module_utils/connectome_spawn/lifecycle.py",
    "line": 198,
    "status": "unreviewed",
    "last_trial_category": "survived",
    "evidence": [],
    "analysis": "Not killed and not equivalent. With need(self.identity_provider is not None, ...) replaced by need(True, ...), the only input that reaches the difference is a Lifecycle whose identity_provider is exactly None on a transition with identity effects. The very next statement (lifecycle.py:199) passes that None to validate_provider_name, whose first action reads provider.supports_rename (identity.py:38), so the mutated run always raises AttributeError where the oracle raises SpawnError('identity provider required'). Nothing is evaluated between lines 198 and 199 that a fake adapter, importer or persisted state could turn into a declared refusal (the name argument is a plain lookup in already validated records), and nothing is written in either run, so there is no clean kill; the exception class differs, so it is not equivalent. A crash-only vector is not possible either: the guard sits in the method Lifecycle.transition, which needs a constructed Lifecycle instance, and no module-level function of the oracle calls transition (cli.main and the shim only call status). Tried: every target with identity effects (initiation, named, clean active, retired with a live handle); all crash at line 199."
  },
